1
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:06,920
Don't worry, Alexandra.

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:07,970
We'll find the owner.

3
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:09,710
How, Robbie?

4
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:11,570
Let me think.

5
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:12,740
Gemma, sit.

6
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,970
Good Gemma.

7
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:15,100
Give me your paw.

8
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,450
Good Gemma.

9
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:18,040
This dog is well trained.

10
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,690
She likes you, too.

11
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:21,860
So how are we going to find the owners?

12
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:25,220
With a little help from the ASPCA,

13
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:28,810
the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

14
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:30,020
They're the ones.

15
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,640
We once found a cat.

16
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,600
She was caught in the branches of our tree.

17
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,610
And Dad called the ASPCA.

18
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:37,170
They came and solved the problem.

19
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:43,340
Robbie, let's call them.

20
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:50,910
Let me see -- ASPCA...

21
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:51,490
Here it is.

22
00:00:51,490 --> 00:01:02,030
ASPCA Animal Shelter.

23
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:12,570
555-7700.

24
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:14,680
Hello, ASPCA.

25
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:17,530
Hello, my name is Robbie Stewart.

26
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:19,890
I have a lost dog I'd like to bring to you.

27
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:21,120
How late are you open?

28
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,040
We're open till nine P.M.

29
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:23,580
Thank you.

30
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,230
I'll bring the dog over by nine.

31
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:25,910
Thanks.

32
00:01:25,910 --> 00:01:27,300
Bye.

33
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:27,710
Thanks.

34
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:36,490
Good-bye.

35
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:38,010
They're still open?

36
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:39,040
They're open until nine o'clock.

37
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:41,150
We have two and a half hours.

38
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:42,440
Let's take Gemma by there now.

39
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,010
They'll find the owner.

40
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:46,610
I hope so.

41
00:01:46,610 --> 00:01:49,990
I'm so sad to see this little dog without her family.

42
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:52,630
I'm sure they'll find the owner.

43
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:55,500
But if they don't, I'll adopt her.

44
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:59,350
She's so cute.

45
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:02,290
Look at those eyes.

46
00:02:02,290 --> 00:02:03,740
She's hard to resist.

47
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:07,350
Don't you just love her?

48
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,430
I'd like to keep her, too.

49
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:11,000
But I'll be going home to Greece

50
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,610
at the end of the semester.

51
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:19,400
She just wants love and affection.

52
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,070
Come on, Robbie.

53
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:21,720
Let's get her to the animal shelter,

54
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,880
so they can find her owners quickly.

55
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,060
Don't worry, Gemma.

56
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:27,840
We'll get you home.

57
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:30,270
It's not easy being away from home.

58
00:02:30,270 --> 00:02:31,680
Come on, poochie.

59
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,330
Atta girl!

60
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:35,590
Let's go.

61
00:02:35,590 --> 00:03:01,040
We're off to the animal shelter.

62
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,010
Your name?

63
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:03,480
Robbie Stewart.

64
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,900
And this is Alexandra Pappas.

65
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:10,800
Your name will do, Mr. Stewart.

66
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:14,840
Your address?

67
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:18,870
46 Linden street, Riverdale.

68
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,530
Where did you find the dog?

69
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:22,110
She found us.

70
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:24,160
You tried calling the number on the collar?

71
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:27,610
Yes, but the number's no longer in service.

72
00:03:27,610 --> 00:03:29,850
And there's no address on the dog tag?

73
00:03:29,850 --> 00:03:32,240
There's no other information.

74
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,990
No ID number.

75
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:37,740
Without that, it's hard.

76
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:40,180
You will try to find the dog's owner.

77
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,380
Oh, we'll try, believe me.

78
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,340
And if you don't?

79
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:47,230
Yes?

80
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:50,970
If you don't ... can I ... can I adopt the dog?

81
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:52,150
Why, yes.

82
00:03:52,150 --> 00:03:54,850
If the owners don't claim the dog in forty-eight hours,

83
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:56,870
then you can apply for adoption.

84
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:58,060
How do I do that?

85
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,560
You really want to?

86
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,390
Yes, I'm serious.

87
00:04:01,390 --> 00:04:03,110
If no one comes to claim Gemma,

88
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:05,060
I'd like to adopt her.

89
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:08,060
It's not difficult.
